diagnostic_evidence.quote:
The key point is to check that $F$ is well defined as a continuous map from
    $[0,1]\times G$ to $\T$, i.e., for every $\tau\in [0,1]$ and $\gamma\in\mathcal{P}$
    \begin{equation}\label{well-def}
      F\left( \tau, c_\gamma (1-0)\right)=F\left( \tau, c_\gamma(0)\right).
    \end{equation}
